# Registry mirrors: curated entries only. Schema per line:
#   <https-url> <id> kind=pip owner=<owner> docs=<docs-url> tier=<tier> verified=<status>
# tier official-default = the origin itself: NEVER auto-selected as a mirror,
#   offered only as "reset to official" via explicit --mirror <official-URL>.
# tier optional = third-party mirror: default auto-pick, still behind
#   --with-registry plus typed confirmation.
# Plain http:// URLs are rejected by the modules (HTTPS only).
# verified=pending blocks use (see docs/DATA-REVIEW.md); only the maintainer
# flips it to verified after manual review. Never set it yourself.
# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
https://pypi.org/simple/ pypi-main kind=pip owner=Python-Software-Foundation docs=https://pypi.org tier=official-default verified=pending
https://mirror-pypi.runflare.com/simple/ runflare-ir kind=pip owner=Runflare docs=https://runflare.com tier=optional verified=pending
